<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/004L">Example <span data-tag="004L">11.6.0.217</span>.</a> The contents of this tag are now contained in Proposition <a data-tag="004H" href="/tag/004H">1.4.5.7</a>. </p>
<p>Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category. Then the homotopy category $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$ constructed in Definition <a data-tag="004C" href="/tag/004C">1.4.5.3</a> is also a homotopy category of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="004J" href="/tag/004J">1.3.6.1</a>. More precisely, the map $u: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} )$ of Construction <a data-tag="004G" href="/tag/004G">1.4.5.6</a> exhibits $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$ as a homotopy category of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, by virtue of Proposition <a data-tag="004H" href="/tag/004H">1.4.5.7</a>. </p>
